      "id": 1,
      "text": "Indian Lake was founded in 1965 as a private residential community built around a 326‑acre reservoir on Brush Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/indian_lake_missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Indian Lake Property Owners Association, formed by residents, manages the lake and coordinates restoration projects with University of Missouri limnologists.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://ilpoa.org/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community lies roughly 5 miles northwest of Cuba and is surrounded by the Mark Twain National Forest, offering a secluded family‑oriented retreat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indian_Lake%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fish from Indian Lake are considered safe to eat, with no current advisories as of 2024 after past chlordane testing in 1986.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/indian_lake_missouri",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Indian Lake’s shoreline stretches about five miles, providing ample space for boating, fishing, and swimming within a forested Ozark setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
